"Edrobot" <Ed_the_robot@yahoo.com> writes:
> How do I make a race for Nethack?

Assuming that you've using an existing base monster or have already
added it into monst.c (if you need advice on that, it exists), the
process of turning it into a playable race is as follows:

First, add an entry into the races[] struct in role.c. For example,
the existing elven entry is:

{       "elf", "elven", "elvenkind", "Elf",
        {0, 0},
        PM_ELF, NON_PM, PM_ELF_MUMMY, PM_ELF_ZOMBIE,
        MH_ELF | ROLE_MALE|ROLE_FEMALE | ROLE_CHAOTIC,
        MH_ELF, MH_ELF, MH_ORC,
        /*  Str    Int Wis Dex Con Cha */
        {    3,     3,  3,  3,  3,  3 },
        {   18,    20, 20, 18, 16, 18 },
        /* Init   Lower  Higher */
        {  1, 0,  0, 1,  1, 0 },        /* Hit points */
        {  2, 0,  3, 0,  3, 0 }         /* Energy */
},

This specifies, in turn, the name, adjective, collective noun
(currently unused), and filecode; any difference in individual names
between male and female (for "You feel like a new man!" messages and
the like); the monster a male member of the race corresponds to,
likewise a female (if different, which none presently are), and the
matching mummy and zombie monsters; the MH_FOO corresponding to the
matching M2_FOO flag that denotes a monster of an allied breed (for
things like same-race sacrifice), the genders allowed to play that
race, and the alignments allowed to play that race; the M2_FOO flag
again (I can't see any case in which this would differ), monster types
inclined to be peaceful, and monster types inclined to be hostile;
maxima and minima for the six attributes; and racial modifiers for
initial HP and power and the increases they receive at levelgain (see
hppw-343.txt for how those are applied).

Define MH_FOO equal to M2_FOO in include/monflag.h. Add MH_FOO to the
roles[] entries to specify which roles are valid choices for this
race.  If you want any racial intrinsics, add them to the innate
struct in attrib.c, and add the appropriate line to the Race_switch in
adj_abil(). Look at the other Race_switches to see if you want to do
anything for them too (currently, elves and orcs getting a bonus to
using their respective bows'n'arrows in throw_obj(), and
racial-specific starting gear and preknowledge in u_init()).

That's all the basic setup, I think; then, if you want to make your
race special, you'll want to add Race_if(PM_FOO)-triggered cases in
the situations where they do special things.

> Is making a Nethack race easy for a beginner?

Probably not, no.

